# removed 2026-08-13: Dockerfile, Makefile, main.py, app.py
#
# these were ignored while unfinished so the public repo showed only finished work
# they are graded deliverables now, so they have to be committed
#
# two traps, both silent:
#   1. a pattern with NO SLASH matches at EVERY depth
#      `Dockerfile` also hid api/Dockerfile, web/Dockerfile, monitoring/Dockerfile
#      `app.py` also hid web/app.py and monitoring/app.py
#      committing with those rules would have published a repo with no application in it
#   2. git status says nothing about ignored files -- they are not untracked, so
#      nothing warns you
#      check with:  git status --ignored --short
#                   git check-ignore -v <path>
